            <ArticleTitle>The Modular (Marmor) knee: case report with a minimum follow-up of 2 years.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A follow-up of 2 years or more on 105 patients with the Modular (Marmor) knee replacement revealed that 88 per cent of the patients had a successful result. The complications and failures are analyzed in depth. Late loosening of the components was not observed except with the 6 mm tibial plateau. Pain relief was dramatic as well as improved function, stability and motion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
